00:58:27.782 --> 00:58:35.782
And our freedom is very, very limited. If you are in Islam, then you must be... come out like everybody else.

00:58:35.782 --> 00:58:42.582
There's no such a thing, you know. So that's the way, the philosophy of the Goy Ugoz.

00:58:42.582 --> 00:59:02.082
We, as Jews, we reject this. We believe that not only the substance, matter as such, is the creation of God, not only that God made from zero something with three dimensions called matter, but also all the laws, even the most basic laws of the universe, were created by God.

00:59:02.082 --> 00:59:12.082
What does it mean that they were created by God? It means that God, as a free author, made these laws, He could change them whenever He wishes.

00:59:12.082 --> 00:59:24.642
For us, the miracle, the next, is the proof, is evidence to the fact that God, author of the laws of nature, could change them whenever He wishes.

00:59:24.642 --> 00:59:34.322
He is the absolute master of the universe. There is nothing that in any way restricts, controls, or limits His absolute power.

00:59:34.322 --> 00:59:42.282
Notice, God is not the pilot driving a jet, as the Goa would say.

00:59:42.282 --> 00:59:46.162
Which, a pilot driving a jet, of course, cannot use the jet as a submarine.

00:59:46.162 --> 00:59:52.082
In a way, the pilot who's driving this jet is limited by the jet.

00:59:52.082 --> 00:59:58.082
And the Goa conceived God as, say, a big pilot, a big scientist controlling, you know, the universe.

00:59:58.082 --> 00:59:59.982
But the universe is what it is, and God cannot do it.

01:00:00.000 --> 01:00:13.260
So, we say no. God is in no way controlled by the universe. And therefore we begin with the first thing,

01:00:13.260 --> 01:00:22.660
bereshith, V'al Elohim, eta shamayim v'a'aret. And we don't mean the material heaven and the material earth,

01:00:22.660 --> 01:00:31.660
But we mean rather the laws, even the laws, the basic laws governing this universe are the dictation of God, an example of it.

01:00:31.660 --> 01:00:38.660
There was Hosea, there was darkness, absolute darkness. And then God creates light.

01:00:38.660 --> 01:00:47.660
So, if you have light, today you say, if you have light, naturally, of course, there is no darkness.

01:00:47.660 --> 01:00:51.660
There is no darkness. There cannot be light and darkness together. That's obvious.

01:00:51.660 --> 01:00:54.660
But Qamil al-Tora tells you something very very deep. He says,

01:00:54.660 --> 01:00:57.660
Bayabdel Elohim bina Oru bina Hosek.

01:00:57.660 --> 01:01:03.660
This, that there is light and darkness cannot be together, this is also a creation of God.

01:01:03.660 --> 01:01:07.660
If God would have wanted there could be dark and light together. How? We don't know.

01:01:07.660 --> 01:01:10.660
Our mind today does not operate according to those laws. You see?

01:01:10.660 --> 01:01:13.660
But even bayabdel Elohim bina Oru bina Hosek.

01:01:13.660 --> 01:01:28.660
Even the very contradiction between light and darkness, this contradiction, it is not an accident, it is not nature or unnecessary so. It is also the creation of God.

01:01:28.660 --> 01:01:38.660
So without creation of God, everything would have been tohu v'vohu. God created the world.

01:01:38.660 --> 01:01:57.929
In its first state without laws of nature the whole universe was in a complete chaos because there was no laws of nature to govern this universe And the laws of nature came as a step further

01:01:57.929 --> 01:02:09.929
It's very important. Now, if we accept the thesis of the Tora, then the whole Judaism is very clear. Even if I cannot understand why I have to put the fili,

01:02:09.929 --> 01:02:17.929
